course: dictionary
lesson: 3150
title: Words from a campfire
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ember is a small piece of wood or coal that is still glowing hot after a fire has died down. You can work this out from the words around it. «Hidden embers can stay hot for many hours and start a wildfire.» The clues are stay hot and start a wildfire, so an ember is something still hot that can set other things alight.
explain: «A boy ran around the campfire playing tag and tripped; his hand landed in the embers.» He needed treatment for burns, so embers can hurt you even when there are no flames. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: The word also appears in phrases like «glowing embers» and «the dying embers». Glowing tells you the embers shine with heat, and dying tells you the fire is going out but the hot bits are still there.
fact: An ember is a small piece of wood or coal that is still glowing hot after a fire has died down.
fact: «Embers» is the plural, so it means more than one ember.
fact: «Glowing embers» means hot pieces that are still shining after the fire has died down.
fact: Embers can stay hot under the ash for many hours, so they can start new fires.
fact: To put out a campfire, pour water on it, stir it, and keep going until it is cold to the touch.
exercise: «Embers can stay hot under the ash for many hours.» What are embers? | A type of camping tent | Cold grey ash from a bonfire | *Small pieces of wood or coal still glowing hot after a fire | Smoke rising from a chimney
exercise: «The dying embers» is a phrase. What does it mean? | Water used to put out a fire | A fire that has just been lit | *The last hot bits of a fire that is going out | A big bonfire at a party
exercise: «A boy tripped and his hand landed in the embers.» What does this tell you about embers? | They are soft and cold | They float up into the sky | *They can burn you | They are only found in cities
test: «Hidden embers can stay hot for many hours and start a wildfire.» What does hidden suggest? | Floating on water | *Out of sight, under the ash | Made of plastic | Bright and shining in the sun
test: How should you put out a campfire safely? | *Pour water on it, stir it, and repeat until it is cold | Throw more wood on it | Blow hard on it to make it bigger | Leave it burning all night
exam: In «the dying embers», which word is the clue that the fire is going out? | *dying | the | embers | phrase
</br>
